==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|em|brown}}.  Akin to Italian, {{m|en|imbrunire}}, French {{m|fr|embrunir}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make [[brown]] or [[dusky]].
#* '''1825''', [[w:Walter Scott|Walter Scott]], ''The Talisman'', A. L. Burt Company (1832?), 26:
#*: His features were small, well-formed, and delicate, though deeply '''embrowned''' by the Eastern sun, and terminated by a flowing and curled black beard, which seemed trimmed with peculiar care.
#* '''1864''', Elizabeth Gaskell, ''Cousin Phillis''
#*: He was looking quite a different man to what I had left him; '''embrowned''', sparkles in his eyes, so languid before.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become [[brown]] or [[dusky]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[darken]], make [[dark]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[darken]], become [[dark]].

